  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `nums` containing **distinct** numbers, and you can perform the following operations **until the array is empty**:\n\n* If the first element has the **smallest** value, remove it\n* Otherwise, put the first element at the **end** of the array.\n\nOutput *an integer denoting the number of operations it takes to make* `nums` *empty.*\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [3,4,-1]\nOutput: 5\n```\n\n| Operation | Array |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 | [4, -1, 3] |\n| 2 | [-1, 3, 4] |\n| 3 | [3, 4] |\n| 4 | [4] |\n| 5 | [] |\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,4,3]\nOutput: 5\n```\n\n| Operation | Array |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 | [2, 4, 3] |\n| 2 | [4, 3] |\n| 3 | [3, 4] |\n| 4 | [4] |\n| 5 | [] |\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3]\nOutput: 3\n```\n\n| Operation | Array |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 | [2, 3] |\n| 2 | [3] |\n| 3 | [] |\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= nums.length <= 105`\n* `-109 <= nums[i] <= 109`\n* All values in `nums` are **distinct**.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
